-- statement:
--   **The command loop.**
--
--   The following holds (Lean statement, in the scope of module `Solutions.J6SegILSlab3`):
--
--   ```lean
--   theorem J6Seg.Slab.cmdLoop_runs (H : UnitsOK (I := I) (iprog := iprog) lin OkU OkA KG g dr rd it bk cdr crd cit cbk)
--       (s : IState HS) (G : Fin HS → List ℤ) (hK : ∀ C CU OP ARG ACC, KG (skS G C CU OP ARG ACC)) (hA : G lA = []) (hC : G lC = []) (hD : G lD = [])
--       {m : ℕ} {LM : List ℤ} (hM : G rM = (m : ℤ) :: LM) (cs : List (ℤ × ℤ)) {LN : List ℤ}
--       (hN : G rNC = (cs.length : ℤ) :: LN) {Ba : ℕ} (hcs : CmdsOK OkA Ba cs) (n : ℕ)
--       (hV : VC n cs 0) (RC CU OP ARG ACC : List ℤ) (inp tmp : List U) (hlen : n * m ≤ inp.length)
--       (hok : ∀ u ∈ inp, OkU u) :
--       IRuns I iprog (cmdLoop dr rd it bk)
--         (encK s (lin inp tmp (skS G (flatC cs ++ RC) CU OP ARG ACC)))
--         (encK s (lin (inp.drop (nDrop cs * m)) tmp
--           (skS G RC ((flatC cs).reverse ++ CU) OP ARG ((runC m g cs inp).reverse ++ ACC))))
--         ((cs.length + 1) * (cmdC m Ba (cdr + crd + cit + cbk) + 3000))
--   ```
--
--   **Context.** B-line IL, B1 (streaming slab pass) §3: one command, the command loop, one block
--
--   The skeleton contents are kept in the form `skS G C CU OP ARG ACC` (control `rC`, used
--   commands `rCU`, current op `rOP`, current argument `rARG`, output `rACC`, over `G`).
--
--   * `cmdP`: pop `(op, arg)` from `rC` to `rOP`, `rARG`; branch on the sign of `op`:
--     drop a slab (`op < 0`), emit `m` zeros (`op = 0`), emit the slab mapped by `g arg`, reading
--     the units to the temps and moving them back (`op > 0`); push `op`, `arg` to `rCU`.
--     **`cmd_runs`**.
--   * `cmdLoop`: `rptX rNC cmdP` — the whole command list; **`cmdLoop_runs`**: the output is
--     `runC m g cs inp` (reversed onto `rACC`), the input loses `nDrop cs` slabs.
--   * `restLoop`: `rptX rNC (mv rCU rC; mv rCU rC)` restores the control list.
--     **`restLoop_runs`**.
--   * `blockP = cmdLoop; restLoop`: **`block_runs`**.
--
